WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:03.010
Hi, Mystery Recapped here.

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:09.360
Today I am going to explain the British science
fiction film called “Frequencies.”

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.469
Spoilers ahead!

00:00:10.469 --> 00:00:16.680
Watch out and take care!

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:21.720
The movie is set in a dystopian world where
every person emits a specific frequency which

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:26.789
determines his or her luck, further determining
his or her success in life.

00:00:26.789 --> 00:00:31.000
Higher frequency means better luck and thus
less feelings.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.070
The movie starts as we see some students standing
in a single line; each holding a single green

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:37.070
apple.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:41.380
Marie Curie Fortune, a bright young girl,
is one of the students in the line.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:46.020
The student behind her drops his apple and
she very calmly returns it back to him.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:50.270
The scene then cuts to the students sitting
at their desks preparing for an exam as their

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:53.610
teacher gives them instructions and tells
them to begin.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:58.650
Just then, all the students put on their respective
blindfolds and begin working on the test.

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:02.910
After the test is over, the teacher announces
their names individually and hands them their

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:03.910
results.

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:07.070
Outside, the students discuss the result among
themselves.

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:12.650
Marie Curie proudly boasts her score of 127
while her friends receive scores far lower

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:13.810
than hers.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:18.719
One of Marie’s arrogant friends then introduces
her to Issac Newton Mitchell, who introduces

00:01:18.719 --> 00:01:20.899
himself to Marie as Zak.

00:01:20.899 --> 00:01:24.079
Marie is told that Zak has a frequency of
minus 7.

00:01:24.079 --> 00:01:29.090
The arrogant friend wanted them to meet as
they have exact opposite frequencies, extreme

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:31.010
high and extreme low.

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:34.319
As they stare at each other, it starts raining
abruptly.

00:01:34.319 --> 00:01:37.939
The teacher then calls Zack as her mother
had come to meet ger.

00:01:37.939 --> 00:01:42.439
It turns out that high frequency people and
low frequency people repel each other.

00:01:42.439 --> 00:01:47.149
From the moment Zak met Marie to the time
the teacher calls Zak back was exactly one

00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:51.439
minute, which means they can only be in contact
for not more than one minute.

00:01:51.439 --> 00:01:54.920
Marie’s parents are concerned that their
daughter will never be like other children

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.329
because of her complete lack of empathy.

00:01:57.329 --> 00:01:59.939
They visit one of her teachers to discuss
their queries.

00:01:59.939 --> 00:02:05.020
The teacher clears that because of her extremely
high frequency and high luck, she has less

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.020
feelings.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:09.580
When asked if she can live a normal life like
others, the teacher says that it won't be

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.600
possible at all.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.550
Fastforward into the future and we see an
older teenage Marie presenting her science

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:18.310
project to the same teacher; Miss Anderson.

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:22.911
It is a device that can analyse frequencies
of 2 opposite sex people and tell if they

00:02:22.911 --> 00:02:24.390
are compatible or not.

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:28.860
The therapist praises her ingenuity and says
that it might also help people make friends

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:31.140
and that she herself should try to use it.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:35.300
This prompts Marie to then perform several
experiments to find out whether two people

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:40.090
with very different frequencies can ever have
a meaningful connection or if there is a way

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.580
for someone to increase their frequency.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:47.100
She chooses a test subject that has a frequency
on the lower end of the spectrum; Zak.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:51.490
In the first experiment, she interrogates
Zak who is very awkward with the answers.

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:56.970
As the clock ticks 60 seconds, an aeroplane
starts dropping luggage onto Zak, which he

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:58.290
narrowly evades.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:03.140
Thus, proving the theory that 2 people from
extreme opposite frequencies cant stay together

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:04.560
for more than a minute.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:09.010
Miss Anderson comes onto the scene and warns
Marie that frequencies cannot be changed.

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:14.000
In the subsequent experiments, she meets Zak
for exactly one minute and catalogues everything

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.280
that he says to her.

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:19.520
It is clear from his behaviour that Zak is
interested in Marie but can never seem to

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:20.830
get across to her.

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:25.680
Also, in each of the experiments, the duo
get separated before the 1 minute threshold.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:30.370
Finally, Zak confesses that he loves her and
asks her if she feels that same.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:34.930
She responds by saying that she is incapable
of feeling anything because of her condition.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:39.910
She continues that she shows emotions only
to pretend in front of others.

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:44.470
However, her goal is to one day feel emotions.

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:48.600
The movie then again fast forwards in time;
this time to when Marie is an adult.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:52.980
It shows how her daily life plays out with
her performing everyday tasks in the same

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:54.700
emotionless state.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:58.850
When she is resting at home, her friends and
family come over to give her a surprise birthday

00:03:58.850 --> 00:03:59.850
party.

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:02.730
She sits alone during the party until she
is approached by Zak.

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:06.990
They talk briefly until Zak reminds her that
the clock has crossed 60 seconds.

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:11.300
He then says that he has found a way to help
her and thus she agrees to meet with him.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.740
Later, the duo meet at a place.

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:18.289
Zak reveals that he lasted more than a minute
the last time because he increased his frequency.

00:04:18.289 --> 00:04:22.219
He then tells Marie that there is a way for
her to be able to connect with other people;

00:04:22.219 --> 00:04:24.180
by lowering her energy levels.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:29.069
He explains that it will require physical
contact.

00:04:29.069 --> 00:04:33.580
She is skeptical at first but since she is
eager to experience some form of emotions,

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:37.780
she lays her hand on the table and then Zak
grasps it in his.

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:42.900
Marie is completely overwhelmed, she feels
something but cannot describe it because she

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:45.599
doesn’t know what it feels like to experience
emotion.

00:04:45.599 --> 00:04:50.569
She feels unwell and lets go of his hand but
realises that holding hands had actually made

00:04:50.569 --> 00:04:51.919
her feel better.

00:04:51.919 --> 00:04:55.840
Since they have been talking for way more
than the designated 60 seconds, nature begins

00:04:55.840 --> 00:05:00.300
to rebel and Marie, feeling overwhelmed, kisses
Zak.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.930
We then experience the story from Zak’s
perspective.

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:07.169
The boy at the beginning who dropped the apple
was Zak himself and he liked Marie from the

00:05:07.169 --> 00:05:08.169
start.

00:05:08.169 --> 00:05:11.870
When the teacher calls in Zak from the playground
to meet his mother, it was so that they could

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:15.199
discuss his future in the institute with Miss
Anderson.

00:05:15.199 --> 00:05:19.639
She recommends that Zak be shifted to a different
facility because his frequency is too low

00:05:19.639 --> 00:05:22.139
and that he will never fit in with the others.

00:05:22.139 --> 00:05:23.999
Zak adamantly refuses.

00:05:23.999 --> 00:05:27.719
After the ordeal, Zak makes his way to Theo's
house, his only friend.

00:05:27.719 --> 00:05:31.880
When he gets to the house he is met by Theo’s
father who shows him that he has skills different

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:35.909
from everyone else's because of his ability
to use imagination.

00:05:35.909 --> 00:05:40.190
This is manifested when he finds that he is
excellent with the piano, because of his ability

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:45.889
to see the piano progressions.

00:05:45.889 --> 00:05:49.919
With Theo, he learns that he cannot be with
Marie because a high energy person and a low

00:05:49.919 --> 00:05:54.870
energy person create magnetic fields that
repel each other and cause destruction.

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:59.560
The movie then fast forwards to Zak’s teenage
years where he, like Marie, is presenting

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:01.319
a project at the science fair.

00:06:01.319 --> 00:06:04.860
Marie comes to his station and asks to meet
him after school.

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:07.099
Both of them clearly have different agendas.

00:06:07.099 --> 00:06:14.279
Marie wants to experiment on Zak while Zak,
determined to improve his frequency, tries

00:06:14.279 --> 00:06:17.159
his best to establish contact with Marie.

00:06:17.159 --> 00:06:21.990
We see that to increase his own frequency,
Zak, with the help of Theo, uses magnets to

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:24.270
temporarily boost his frequency.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:28.389
Zak experimented with different substances
before each meeting with Marie to see which

00:06:28.389 --> 00:06:30.319
would have the most desirable effect.

00:06:30.319 --> 00:06:35.719
However, they didn’t help much as Marie
admitted to feeling nothing for Zak.

00:06:35.719 --> 00:06:37.999
Fast Forward again to when Zak is an adult.

00:06:37.999 --> 00:06:42.189
He presents a groundbreaking theory that redefines
the concept of frequencies.

00:06:42.189 --> 00:06:47.270
He tells the professors that even high frequency
people can experience emotion if they believe

00:06:47.270 --> 00:06:48.270
in it.

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:54.589
Unfortunately for him, no one buys his idea.

00:06:54.589 --> 00:06:57.940
Zak again meets with Theo to find ways to
improve his frequency.

00:06:57.940 --> 00:07:02.090
They experiment with different compounds but
unexpectedly realise that particular sound

00:07:02.090 --> 00:07:05.460
waves can boost frequency for a short period
of time.

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:09.979
To test this hypothesis, he is sent by Theo
to meet Marie at her birthday party.

00:07:09.979 --> 00:07:14.530
While departing, Theo gives him a device with
code words to activate the sound waves, thus

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:17.710
giving him an additional 5 seconds more this
time.

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:21.770
During their conversation, he’s also wearing
a microphone through which he can hear Theo

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:23.490
giving him new words.

00:07:23.490 --> 00:07:26.159
Everything comes back full circle when both
of them kiss.

00:07:26.159 --> 00:07:31.289
The intimacy has the effect of reducing Marie’s
frequency and quelling the revolt of nature.

00:07:31.289 --> 00:07:34.020
The couple then make love for the first time.

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:38.710
All this while, Zak keeps getting the secret
words on his device, which extends his time

00:07:38.710 --> 00:07:41.889
with Marie.

00:07:41.889 --> 00:07:44.220
They begin to spend more time together.

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:48.619
During their time together, Marie experiences
some bouts of unluckiness, such as missing

00:07:48.619 --> 00:07:49.869
her train.

00:07:49.869 --> 00:07:52.869
This is a clear sign that her frequency is
dwindling.

00:07:52.869 --> 00:07:56.819
She then makes a bold move and takes Zak to
visit her parents.

00:07:56.819 --> 00:08:00.610
Her parents, in many ways, are high frequency
individuals like her.

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:04.270
So they are concerned that when an average
boy comes into their house, the frequency

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:07.029
mismatch would cause a rebellion of nature.

00:08:07.029 --> 00:08:11.449
Marie ensures them that it will not happen
and then the entire family has dinner together.

00:08:11.449 --> 00:08:16.089
At the table, Zak explains to Marie’s father
how the concept of harmonizing frequencies

00:08:16.089 --> 00:08:17.089
works.

00:08:17.089 --> 00:08:21.520
He explains that nature will always seek balance
so that high frequency and low frequency people

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:25.830
can be together because the low frequency
individual will receive some of the energy

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:30.289
of the high frequency individual.

00:08:30.289 --> 00:08:33.500
This will cause uniformity and everyone can
be the same level.

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:36.970
He then presents his device to Marie’s father
and explains how it works.

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:41.070
It basically takes the frequency mismatch
between the people in the surroundings and

00:08:41.070 --> 00:08:45.000
presents a two syllable word that can help
balance out the frequency.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:50.250
Marie’s father is very excited to hear that
a device can be used to achieve complete balance.

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:54.380
He believes that the device would render the
concept of high energy and low energy to be

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:57.190
useless, thus giving everyone justice.

00:08:57.190 --> 00:09:01.730
In fact Marie’s father is so confident in
the idea of universal balance that he puts

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:05.380
together a research team to improve the device’s
functionality.

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:08.259
The team consists of some of Zak’s old school
mates.

00:09:08.259 --> 00:09:11.170
However, they soon discover a strange side
effect.

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:17.490
If one asks anyone to do anything after saying
the two syllable word, they will do it involuntarily.

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:22.090
While Zak and Marie’s father try to figure
out how to fix the glitch, Marie comes to

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:26.940
a realization that when Zak met her at her
birthday, he was using carefully selected

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:29.000
words to lower her frequency.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:33.589
Then, with the two syllable word and a meek
request, he subconsciously compelled her to

00:09:33.589 --> 00:09:34.840
fall in love with him.

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:38.530
Marie’s father is furious at Zak for manipulating
her daughter like that.

00:09:38.530 --> 00:09:42.620
To his defence, Zak says that he had no knowledge
of the side effect and that the entire thing

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:47.100
was a misunderstanding.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:51.740
Needless to say, Marie’s father disbands
the team and makes everyone sign a contract

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:54.310
to drop the idea of experimenting with the
device.

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:57.880
He also forbids Zak from seeing Marie again.

00:09:57.880 --> 00:10:01.860
One day, upon returning to his room, Zak finds
some men in his room.

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:03.899
One of the men says that they are from the
government.

00:10:03.899 --> 00:10:06.490
He even has the same device that Zak invented.

00:10:06.490 --> 00:10:11.690
The man then asks Zak three questions and
he can only respond by nodding his head.

00:10:11.690 --> 00:10:15.490
Zak realises that the questions the man was
asking were phrased in such a way that they

00:10:15.490 --> 00:10:17.670
would ensure he was telling the truth.

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:21.470
Zak doesn’t understand how that is possible
because no one else was prive to the work

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:23.269
they had been doing with his device.

00:10:23.269 --> 00:10:25.650
The man then offers Zak a job.

00:10:25.650 --> 00:10:29.270
After Zak reaches the secret place, the man
explains that the government has set up a

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:30.600
secret team.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:34.990
He stresses that the team needs to neutralize
the threat, known as the manual, which is

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:37.680
the name given to the two syllable generator
device.

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:41.810
The team consists of the team that Marie’s
father set up before, since only they knew

00:10:41.810 --> 00:10:42.810
how it worked.

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:46.970
The government agent then tells them the story
of how this technology had surfaced up several

00:10:46.970 --> 00:10:51.670
times in the past and caused devastation but
had always been obscured from the public to

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:53.620
keep the balance and peace.

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:57.690
He knew that it would inevitably be rediscovered
and that, again, they would have to bury it

00:10:57.690 --> 00:10:58.880
in secrecy.

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:03.200
Over the next few days, the team works very
diligently trying to figure out how to overcome

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:04.339
this problem.

00:11:04.339 --> 00:11:09.440
They all put forth their ideas, suggestions
and mathematical models to resolve it but

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:11.070
never make it to a consensus.

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:15.019
Meanwhile, Marie’s father is still cold
to Zak.

00:11:15.019 --> 00:11:19.389
Zak then suggests making an anti manual, one
that is flawed so that its perception in the

00:11:19.389 --> 00:11:23.459
public is tainted and people are less likely
to be inclined to use it.

00:11:23.459 --> 00:11:28.519
Also, he realises that from his study of patterns,
there must be some antidote words to nullify

00:11:28.519 --> 00:11:30.610
the effect of the glitching words.

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:32.920
All of them stick to this theory to try it
out.

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:37.220
They end up producing words that implicate
harmless commands but can only be used once

00:11:37.220 --> 00:11:38.220
every hour.

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:42.269
The government official isn’t pleased to
replace one havoc causing word with another

00:11:42.269 --> 00:11:44.480
and so he bans the words immediately.

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:49.279
Later, at the request of Marie, Zak utters
a word from the device along with a command

00:11:49.279 --> 00:11:51.870
so that Marie will fall out of love with him.

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:54.320
However, she says that nothing’s changed.

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:58.410
When the government agent comes to know that
Zak tried manipulation again, he is locked

00:11:58.410 --> 00:12:01.379
into confinement and is forbidden to speak
with anyone.

00:12:01.379 --> 00:12:05.879
In this state of solitary however, Zak’s
mind begins to wander the depth of his knowledge

00:12:05.879 --> 00:12:10.620
and procure everything he knows on the subject
to find a solution; an antidote.

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:15.130
Thoughts and cacophonous sounds whizz past
his mind until the solution becomes clear

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:16.130
to him.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.930
He knows where to find the antidote.

00:12:17.930 --> 00:12:21.720
Desperate to find the antidote, Zak lures
the guard into his room and utters a single

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:25.959
word that freezes him in place.

00:12:25.959 --> 00:12:27.790
He then escapes the secret facility.

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:31.420
He makes his way to Theo’s father’s home
where he knows he will find the antidote.

00:12:31.420 --> 00:12:35.709
Theo’s dad realises that Zak has figured
it out and offers to help him.

00:12:35.709 --> 00:12:39.829
Marie also arrives at the scene and informs
him that he has less time.

00:12:39.829 --> 00:12:43.709
Just then, the government officials strom
the place and restrain Zak.

00:12:43.709 --> 00:12:47.480
Suddenly, Theo’s dad begins playing a melody
on his piano.

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:51.139
When asked what he is doing, he replies that
he is simply giving them the antidote.

00:12:51.139 --> 00:12:54.329
He then challenges them to use any word while
he is playing.

00:12:54.329 --> 00:12:59.540
The government official does so and to their
surprise, it makes no difference.

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:05.730
Theo’s dad then reveals that when Mozart
plays, everyone is the same frequency.

00:13:05.730 --> 00:13:10.790
He continues by saying that music neutralizes
the power of the words and that Mozart immunized

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:13.560
people against the book that contained the
words.

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:17.519
In short, music resets everything.

00:13:17.519 --> 00:13:21.500
The final segment is shown from Theo’s perspective.

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:26.029
It is revealed that he was the one who dropped
the apple so that Zak could talk to Marie.

00:13:26.029 --> 00:13:29.949
It is also revealed that Theo has exactly
average frequency.

00:13:29.949 --> 00:13:33.500
What follows is an interesting dynamic between
Theo and his dad.

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:37.790
His dad believes that humans can escape the
entrapment of machine like thinking by using

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:40.470
imagination and their concept of free will.

00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:45.750
Theo, on the other hand, believes that all
humans are machines and they can be very predictable.

00:13:45.750 --> 00:13:49.940
All of Theo’s work during the course of
the movie had reflected this very mindset;

00:13:49.940 --> 00:13:54.360
from his helping Zak control frequencies to
his science project that was obstructed by

00:13:54.360 --> 00:13:55.949
the Zak- Marie attraction.

00:13:55.949 --> 00:14:00.230
Elsewhere, Marie and Zak are together and
get their results back from the doctor, who

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:06.040
gives them doses of Mozart, Bach and Pachbell
as medicines.

00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:10.170
The doctor also confirms that Marie’s feelings
are not due to manipulation.

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:14.360
The movie ends on a high note when Theo believes
he has figured out the universal symphony,

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:19.019
a complete knowledge of things that will allow
him to predict how any interaction or event

00:14:19.019 --> 00:14:20.240
is going to happen.

00:14:20.240 --> 00:14:25.490
So, that leaves the question, did anyone in
the movie ever have a free will or were they

00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:31.230
